-- EXPECT-ERROR: expected `Int` but got `String`
-- Monomorphism restriction (2026-07-13): an UNANNOTATED let-bound lambda
-- stays monomorphic — its first use pins its type, so a second use at a
-- different type is rejected. Rationale: generalizing it leaves the
-- compiled closure's apply functions at the erased (tagged) calling
-- convention while callees with concrete fn-typed params call them raw —
-- silently wrong comparisons / SIGBUS (the bench-sort family). Annotate to
-- opt back into polymorphism: `let id : (a) -> a = fn x -> x` (see
-- accept/t03_let_poly). The uniform-apply-ABI follow-up in specs/todos.md
-- will lift this restriction.
mod M do
  fn main() do
    let id = fn x -> x
    println(int_to_string(id(5)))
    println(id("hello"))
  end
end
